WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.810
In July 2008, Zimbabwe's official
inflation rate reached 231

2
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.090
million per cent a year.

3
00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.140
In 2009, people stopped
using the local currency.

4
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.400
Most inflation is far lower.

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.860
But in October 2022, prices in the UK were

6
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.280
rising by 11.1 per cent a year.

7
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.460
So if your pay goes up every year,

8
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.720
can you still end up worse off?

9
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.370
In this mission, you'll build a
price index from a basket of goods,

10
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.000
step by step.

11
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.340
Then you'll find out who wins
and who loses when prices rise.

12
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.940
Your mission: find out what
rising prices really do

13
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.440
to the money in your pocket.
